# Blog — project context

Personal technical blog. Owner writes in `/studio`. The public site reads published rows through RLS.

## Stack

- **Next.js 16** App Router under `src/`
- **Tailwind CSS v4** CSS-first (`src/app/globals.css`, `@theme inline`)
- **shadcn-style** primitives in `src/components/ui/`
- **Supabase** Postgres + Auth (GitHub) + Storage (`media` bucket)
- **Vercel** region `fra1`
- **Supabase** region `eu-central-1`

## Authoritative paths

- `src/app/(site)/` — public reading UI
- `src/app/studio/` — owner CMS (posts, projects, timeline, comments, settings)
- `src/app/(auth)/` — `/login`, `/denied`, `/auth/callback`
- `src/lib/actions/` — Server Actions (Zod + `requireOwner` for writes)
- `src/lib/data/` — public reads with `'use cache'`, `cacheTag`, `cacheLife`
- `src/lib/markdown/` — `renderMarkdown` (preview === publish)
- `src/lib/supabase/` — clients (see below)
- `src/lib/database.types.ts` — generated; do not hand-edit
- `supabase/migrations/` — schema, RLS, grants, functions
- `content/drafts/` — local scratch (gitignored except README)
- `docs/` — architecture, content model, local/dev, deploy, design, performance, security

## Supabase clients

- **Cookie client** (`src/lib/supabase/server.ts`, `browser.ts`) — session CRUD, studio, actions, OAuth callback
- **Anon client** (`src/lib/supabase/anon.ts`) — cookie-less, for `'use cache'` public reads only
- **Service role** (`src/lib/supabase/admin.ts`) — **only** for `scripts/grant-owner.mjs` (and equivalent owner-bootstrap). Never import into App Router pages, actions, or client components.

## Working conventions

- Public pages must not leak drafts, pending comments, or studio data.
- Mutations go through Server Actions + cookie client + RLS. Do not bypass with service role.
- After schema changes, add a timestamped migration and regenerate types with `scripts/gen-types.sh`.
- Regions stay paired: Vercel `fra1`, Supabase `eu-central-1`.
- Read `docs/local-development.md` and `docs/deployment.md` before touching Docker, remote Supabase, or Vercel.
